1
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:09,342
Congrats on graduating!

2
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:11,219
Are you looking at schools?

3
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,347
America or the UK, either works.

4
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:15,264
I support you no matter what.

5
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:17,768
You can stay there
to work afterward.

6
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:19,686
How does that sound?

7
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:22,022
Looks like it's starting.
It's starting!

8
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,482
Hurry up!

9
00:00:24,483 --> 00:00:26,484
It's starting!

10
00:00:26,485 --> 00:00:27,444
Hurry up!

11
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:35,661
<i>I know
I can do well at anything,</i>

12
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:43,168
<i>but is that guaranteed path
to success really what I want?</i>

13
00:00:45,337 --> 00:00:46,838
<i>Or maybe...</i>

14
00:00:47,089 --> 00:00:49,174
<i>I should trust
my gut this time?</i>

15
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:15,450
<i>Someday, you can find
Sunshine, sunshine</i>

16
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,082
<i>Run, run, to hope</i>

17
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:24,250
<i>Hope, hope, don't go</i>

18
00:01:24,251 --> 00:01:26,336
<i>I believe in you someday</i>

19
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:32,384
<i>Someone just like you
Lights up my dream</i>

20
00:01:45,606 --> 00:01:49,234
Huh. Just post a photo,
and it gets over 5,000 likes.

21
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:52,486
- This girl is so popular.
- Trust me.

22
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:55,365
In two months,
I'll revive this restaurant.

23
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:02,414
This is a small restaurant.

24
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:04,332
And I'm always here.

25
00:02:04,333 --> 00:02:06,584
I don't think we need a manager.

26
00:02:06,585 --> 00:02:08,920
He's right. Or if your friends
haven't had enough,

27
00:02:09,171 --> 00:02:11,757
I can treat them
to a real heavy serving.

28
00:02:12,424 --> 00:02:15,886
Bro, can you serve me
a side dish?

29
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:17,721
Why?

30
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,311
Go get it.

31
00:02:26,521 --> 00:02:27,606
Hurry up.

32
00:02:33,195 --> 00:02:34,446
Stop!

33
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:36,907
Do you know what the problem is?

34
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:43,914
Keep your fingers
out of the plates when serving.

35
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:52,964
With so many dishes on the menu,

36
00:02:53,215 --> 00:02:54,674
which one
is your signature dish?

37
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:56,385
All our dishes are delicious.

38
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,888
Customers will never know
how to order.

39
00:03:01,181 --> 00:03:03,892
Make all of them for me.

40
00:03:14,528 --> 00:03:16,320
I've deleted most dishes
that are not cost effective

41
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:17,863
and that nobody orders.

42
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:20,367
We should find
our signature dishes.

43
00:03:21,368 --> 00:03:24,412
These are indeed the dishes
that are losing us money.

44
00:03:24,413 --> 00:03:26,706
Since you're the chef here,

45
00:03:26,707 --> 00:03:30,835
you should go back
to where you belong and think
about what your specialty is.

46
00:03:30,836 --> 00:03:33,171
You can eat 80%
of those dishes at Chang Xin.

47
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:35,966
<i>They have better service,
atmosphere,
and a more upscale setting.</i>

48
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:38,552
To be honest,
if I were a customer today,

49
00:03:38,677 --> 00:03:40,345
why would I come
to your restaurant?

50
00:03:43,515 --> 00:03:46,977
All you need is tasty dishes,
good service,
and brand reliability.

51
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,353
All you've got...

52
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,523
is tasty dishes.

53
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:53,024
I can train you on service.

54
00:03:53,275 --> 00:03:54,985
I'm good at building
brand reliability.

55
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:58,238
All your weaknesses
are what I'm good at.
How's that?

56
00:03:59,531 --> 00:04:02,325
Do you still think
you don't need me?

57
00:04:12,002 --> 00:04:16,047
I'm wondering
why you have to be our manager.

58
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:20,886
My instinct.

59
00:04:27,726 --> 00:04:32,522
I don't know why,
but the fried rice you made
really touched me.

60
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:37,944
Because I feel that...

61
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:45,368
<i>in you and here,
I can find my future.</i>

62
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:49,331
That's my instinct.

63
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:07,766
Guys, this girl, Chao Yi-hsuan,

64
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:09,726
is our new manager here.

65
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:27,661
<i>If you own a restaurant,
you need to eat everywhere.</i>

66
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:29,703
You haven't tried enough.

67
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,998
Let's eat at all
the restaurants around here.

68
00:05:40,924 --> 00:05:43,635
Hi. Here's the menu.
Take your time.

69
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:44,803
Tell me when you're ready
to order.

70
00:05:46,096 --> 00:05:48,098
Thank you.

71
00:05:48,348 --> 00:05:49,891
Your turn. A smile.

72
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:54,396
A smile.

73
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,650
<i>Someday you can...</i>

74
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:01,527
Okay,
maybe that's not your style.

75
00:06:01,528 --> 00:06:02,946
You already look
like a gangster.

76
00:06:03,822 --> 00:06:06,491
And no long face or slouching.

77
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:08,743
<i>You can find
Sunshine, sunshine</i>

78
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:15,375
Have you ordered
seafood pizza?

79
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,334
No.

80
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:17,543
Are you sure?

81
00:06:17,544 --> 00:06:19,503
We said no.

82
00:06:19,504 --> 00:06:21,380
I'm sorry.

83
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:22,674
See?

84
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:24,801
- Have you ordered seafood pizza?
- Yeah.

85
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:29,139
We want braised eggplant,
scrambled eggs with onion,

86
00:06:29,389 --> 00:06:30,557
and Hakka stir-fry.

87
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:31,892
I'm sorry.
Can you say that again?

88
00:06:37,856 --> 00:06:39,858
- I want some water.
- Oh, okay.

89
00:06:40,775 --> 00:06:42,568
- Warm water.
- Okay.

90
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:44,570
Mm-hmm.

91
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:47,948
Excellent service is all about
being one step ahead
of the customer's needs.

92
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:49,950
- Chin-nan...
- Yeah, I'm lame.

93
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,161
I'll make myself better.

94
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:56,540
<i>We need
to differentiate ourselves from
our surrounding restaurants.</i>

95
00:06:56,541 --> 00:07:00,045
<i>So, I hereby
redefine our restaurant
as a Taiwan-style bistro.</i>

96
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:02,588
<i>We need to change
our menu and decoration.</i>

97
00:07:02,589 --> 00:07:04,590
<i>But we've redecorated
not long ago.</i>

98
00:07:04,591 --> 00:07:06,885
<i>Let's give our customers
a breath of fresh air.</i>

99
00:07:13,892 --> 00:07:15,560
JIN LAI HAO

100
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:20,774
Today, we're deciding
on our signature dish.

101
00:07:20,899 --> 00:07:22,650
Why does every customer
have to order it?

102
00:07:22,651 --> 00:07:24,735
That's the story
we'll tell them.

103
00:07:24,736 --> 00:07:27,155
If you tell a good story,
it sells, okay?

104
00:07:31,785 --> 00:07:33,953
Steamed Fish
with Cordia Dichotoma
can be our signature.

105
00:07:33,954 --> 00:07:36,121
I've always wanted
to promote milkfish.

106
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:37,748
It's easy to cook,

107
00:07:37,749 --> 00:07:39,209
but it brings out
the flavor of the ingredients.

108
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:42,212
Plus, it connects me with my dad
and is what got me into cooking.

109
00:07:45,048 --> 00:07:46,674
That's a great story.

110
00:07:46,675 --> 00:07:49,636
But one whole fish
seems too much.

111
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:52,137
Maybe we'll do a fish fillet

112
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:53,765
and present it like
a Western-style fish
<i>en papillote</i> .

113
00:07:56,101 --> 00:07:57,643
Good idea.

114
00:07:57,644 --> 00:07:59,604
I also suggest Three-cup Chicken
be our signature dish.

115
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:01,982
It's a cooking method
unique to Taiwan.

116
00:08:02,107 --> 00:08:05,109
It's easy, efficient to make,
and looks good.

117
00:08:05,110 --> 00:08:06,945
Boss will make
a fish fillet <i>en papillote</i>

118
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:08,779
while Yu-li will make
three-cup chicken.

119
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:10,281
Let's hold an online vote.

120
00:08:14,077 --> 00:08:16,287
<i>Okay. This is our boss,
Chou Lu-yung.</i>

121
00:08:16,538 --> 00:08:18,623
<i>We're preparing
the ingredients now.</i>

122
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:21,251
<i>This is our other chef, Yu-li.</i>

123
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:22,669
<i>Hello!</i>

124
00:08:22,794 --> 00:08:24,295
They're working really hard...

125
00:08:24,546 --> 00:08:27,132
You're in the shot!
We can't use it now.

126
00:08:28,091 --> 00:08:30,927
What are you cooking?

127
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:32,886
<i>Three-cup Chicken!</i>

128
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,764
<i>It smells good.</i>

129
00:08:36,141 --> 00:08:38,143
How to season it?

130
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:42,646
Rice wine.
We're adding rice wine.

131
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:44,024
Yeah, that's rice wine.

132
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:47,569
Good.

133
00:08:53,283 --> 00:08:54,743
<i>Nice!</i>

134
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:06,296
Are you afraid
of the flames, Yu-li?

135
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:13,845
You're afraid of fire?

136
00:09:18,308 --> 00:09:20,101
Does anyone know that?

137
00:09:21,895 --> 00:09:23,313
Who can answer me?

138
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:25,148
Is Yu-li afraid of fire?

139
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:31,863
Tell me.

140
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:33,698
Why did you hire her?

141
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:39,203
I hired her to be a chef.

142
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:41,748
Hired someone
afraid of fire to be a chef?

143
00:09:43,208 --> 00:09:45,084
Yu-li's trained
in Western cooking.

144
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:47,252
They don't use a high flame.

145
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:48,922
We intentionally avoid
such dishes on our menu.

146
00:09:49,047 --> 00:09:51,800
Can't you see our signboard
says "Taiwanese cuisine"?

147
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:56,596
Her stir-fry dishes
are unstable,

148
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:58,680
but except for those,
nothing's wrong with her.

149
00:09:58,681 --> 00:10:02,102
You're telling me
our signature dish
doesn't have to be the best.

150
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,354
A chef who's afraid of fire.

151
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:06,898
<i>I've never heard
anything more absurd.</i>

152
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:09,108
<i>I'm a fish
that's scared of water.</i>

153
00:10:09,109 --> 00:10:11,276
I don't know why you hired her.

154
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:13,904
You can't make a silk purse
out of a sow's ear.

155
00:10:13,905 --> 00:10:14,906
She's not a sow's ear.

156
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:17,742
She has been working hard
for years.

157
00:10:23,248 --> 00:10:25,250
You know,

158
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:29,921
new decoration
and better service
aren't enough.

159
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,966
What determines if we succeed
or fail is the flavor.

160
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:35,385
We need consistent flavor.

161
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:37,761
You hired me as your manager,
so you need to trust
my judgment.

162
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:39,096
With me here,

163
00:10:39,097 --> 00:10:40,931
Jin Lai Hao will only get
bigger and better.

164
00:10:40,932 --> 00:10:42,684
You can't help her forever.

165
00:11:05,707 --> 00:11:07,167
Are you happy here?

166
00:11:09,711 --> 00:11:10,795
Yeah.

167
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:15,258
Do you enjoy working here?

168
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:20,138
Yes, I do.

169
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:24,184
But you've been afraid of fire
for a long while,

170
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:26,978
and you haven't solved
the problem.

171
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:33,234
Everyone here wants Jin Lai Hao
to be better and bigger.

172
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:36,070
But your stir-frying
is too inconsistent,

173
00:11:37,864 --> 00:11:39,449
which will be
a huge problem for us.

174
00:11:40,909 --> 00:11:41,993
You know that, don't you?

175
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:45,496
Yeah.

176
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:53,296
Take it.

177
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:58,843
Boss,

178
00:11:59,344 --> 00:12:00,970
don't do this.

179
00:12:19,364 --> 00:12:20,782
It's this month's salary.

180
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:34,212
Thank you.

181
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:38,758
Thank you for everything.

182
00:12:46,808 --> 00:12:48,101
I've doubled the money.

183
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:53,272
Are you crazy?

184
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:55,108
If you enjoy working here,

185
00:12:56,109 --> 00:12:58,277
I want you to work twice as hard

186
00:12:58,278 --> 00:12:59,862
to make this double pay
worth it.

187
00:13:00,863 --> 00:13:03,240
While we're renovating
the restaurant,

188
00:13:03,241 --> 00:13:05,118
overcome your fear of fire.

189
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:08,997
Can you do that?

190
00:13:15,378 --> 00:13:16,462
Yes, I can.

191
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:19,424
Good.

192
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:22,217
Have you heard
what she has promised me?

193
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:23,803
Wait. Boss...

194
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:26,263
Yeah, one more thing.

195
00:13:26,264 --> 00:13:27,390
Listen.

196
00:13:28,391 --> 00:13:30,225
Working at Jin Lai Hao

197
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:34,271
means you are my partners,
my teammates,

198
00:13:34,272 --> 00:13:35,606
and my family.

199
00:13:40,028 --> 00:13:43,031
So, whatever happens,

200
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,908
I'll never give up my partners,

201
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:49,287
my teammates or my family.

202
00:13:51,331 --> 00:13:52,540
That's what I believe.

203
00:13:55,585 --> 00:13:59,464
If anyone doesn't enjoy working
here and decides to leave,

204
00:13:59,589 --> 00:14:01,340
tell me immediately.

205
00:14:01,341 --> 00:14:02,467
I won't force you to stay.

206
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:11,100
Good.

207
00:14:12,477 --> 00:14:14,228
If you want
to keep working with me,

208
00:14:15,313 --> 00:14:16,981
let's not give up
on one another.

209
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:20,985
Yi-hsuan,

210
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:23,446
you're our manager.

211
00:14:24,572 --> 00:14:26,115
I want you to help Yu-li.

212
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:32,372
Got it.

213
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:43,173
<i>Okay. This is our boss,
Chou Lu-yung.</i>

214
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:46,176
<i>This is our other chef, Yu-li.</i>

215
00:14:46,177 --> 00:14:47,470
<i>You're in the shot!</i>

216
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:53,184
<i>Okay. This is our boss,
Chou Lu-yung.</i>

217
00:14:55,061 --> 00:14:57,230
<i>Okay. This is our boss,
Chou Lu-yung.</i>

218
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,330
<i>My co-workers
in Jin Lai Hao</i>

219
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:17,208
are my teammates,

220
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:18,418
my family.

221
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:21,212
Let's not give up one another.

222
00:15:22,672 --> 00:15:24,172
<i>That's what I believe.</i>

223
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:26,550
<i>I don't know
if a guy saying that</i>

224
00:15:26,551 --> 00:15:29,136
<i>is naive</i>

225
00:15:29,137 --> 00:15:31,556
<i>or just plain stupid.</i>

226
00:15:31,681 --> 00:15:34,225
<i>He's old enough, and he still
trusts others like that?</i>

227
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:39,230
<i>My parents left me
when I was little.</i>

228
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:43,734
<i>How could I believe family
never gives up on each other?</i>

229
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:50,575
<i>But...</i>

230
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:54,161
<i>Why do I feel like</i>

231
00:15:54,162 --> 00:15:56,372
<i>I'm starting to envy</i>

232
00:15:57,457 --> 00:15:59,166
<i>that kind
of wholehearted trust?</i>

233
00:15:59,167 --> 00:16:03,087
Guys, this girl, Chao Yi-hsuan,

234
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,548
is our new manager here.

235
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:09,594
<i>Am I...</i>

236
00:16:26,027 --> 00:16:27,570
<i>Could it be...</i>

237
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:31,491
Have some fruit.

238
00:16:33,618 --> 00:16:35,285
You entered without knocking.

239
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:37,163
Where are the manners
you taught me?

240
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:43,586
My well-mannered daughter,
have some fruit.

241
00:16:45,755 --> 00:16:48,132
- What are you doing?
- Editing a video.

242
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:54,179
We're holding a poll
to decide on our signature dish.

243
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,473
You're still taking
that kind of job?

244
00:16:56,474 --> 00:16:58,642
Is it an ad?

245
00:16:58,643 --> 00:17:01,437
No, I'm working at a restaurant.

246
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:05,816
What? You're working
part-time at a restaurant?

247
00:17:06,067 --> 00:17:08,319
I'm not working part-time.
I'm a manager.

248
00:17:09,654 --> 00:17:12,740
A restaurant manager
is a part-timer in some way.

249
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,494
Don't be a know-it-all.

250
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:20,121
Hey, I've owned a pub
for more than 20 years.

251
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:23,250
The food industry is tough,
low-paid, and looked down upon.

252
00:17:23,251 --> 00:17:25,628
You can do anything
but run a restaurant.

253
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:28,714
Mom, this is what I want to do.

254
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:36,721
CHOU LU-YUNG
MANAGER AND CHEF

255
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:38,683
- You're in love
with the boy?
- No.

256
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,689
You're smart,
pretty and popular online.

257
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:48,441
You should make good use
of your strengths.

258
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:50,570
Tina, I'm interested
in the catering industry.

259
00:17:50,695 --> 00:17:53,030
I'm developing my new career.

260
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:56,367
And I think I'll move out
for a while.

261
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:58,744
Move out?

262
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:01,371
Mom, I'm different from you.

263
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:03,833
I want both love and career.

264
00:18:11,507 --> 00:18:12,466
Why are you here?

265
00:18:13,551 --> 00:18:15,219
Boss asked me to watch you.

266
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:17,722
From now on, I'll live with you.

267
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:19,348
Huh?

268
00:18:19,724 --> 00:18:21,726
I don't know why
you're afraid of fire.

269
00:18:21,851 --> 00:18:24,227
I don't care,
and I don't want to hear it.

270
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:28,482
From today on, I'll watch you
until you're not afraid of it.

271
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:31,193
If you can't do it,
just get lost.

272
00:18:32,403 --> 00:18:33,778
Don't just stand there.

273
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:35,197
I need a place to sleep.

274
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:37,241
Sleep?

275
00:18:37,617 --> 00:18:41,620
- But this is my place.
- Why isn't there
an elevator?

276
00:18:41,621 --> 00:18:42,747
Hey, you...

277
00:18:44,624 --> 00:18:45,583
Wait!

278
00:19:00,598 --> 00:19:02,600
Here. Taste it.

279
00:19:02,725 --> 00:19:03,809
Thank you, sir.

280
00:19:14,362 --> 00:19:15,446
Hsiu-wen,

281
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:20,284
I think you know
the police took Chien-wu
back to the station.

282
00:19:21,369 --> 00:19:22,620
I've heard about it.

283
00:19:26,791 --> 00:19:28,584
Do you know
what restaurant it was?

284
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:32,963
It's Jin Lai Hao.

285
00:19:38,803 --> 00:19:40,638
How strange.

286
00:19:40,763 --> 00:19:43,808
Fate always brings
your old friend and me together.

287
00:19:43,933 --> 00:19:45,393
He's involved in everything.

288
00:19:48,813 --> 00:19:52,483
Hsiu-wen, what do you think
about Chou Lu-yung?

289
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:01,659
He is all nerve and no brain.

290
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:04,494
He doesn't know
how to make a plan.

291
00:20:04,495 --> 00:20:07,498
Being a chef is for him,
not being an owner.

292
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:08,874
Really?

293
00:20:10,209 --> 00:20:13,878
I heard he's renovating
his restaurant.

294
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:17,425
If my memory is right,
it was opened not long ago.

295
00:20:19,635 --> 00:20:20,886
I have no idea.

296
00:20:24,932 --> 00:20:26,892
That's not right.

297
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:30,521
You should stay
in touch with him.

298
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:33,356
Call each other
and catch up on things.

299
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:34,858
That's how it should be.

300
00:20:34,859 --> 00:20:38,696
After all,
you're old friends, right?

301
00:20:52,877 --> 00:20:54,003
Hello.

302
00:20:55,963 --> 00:20:58,339
Hey. Why are you here?

303
00:20:58,340 --> 00:20:59,759
I heard you were renovating
the restaurant.

304
00:20:59,884 --> 00:21:01,343
I'm here to see how it's going.

305
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:03,554
They've started inside.

306
00:21:04,597 --> 00:21:05,973
I'm thinking
about what to do with these.

307
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,894
Keep them. They're growing well.

308
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:11,896
Hey.

309
00:21:24,033 --> 00:21:25,951
Why don't you introduce us?

310
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:30,914
Oh. Sorry.

311
00:21:30,915 --> 00:21:34,251
This is Wu Hsiu-wen,
my high school classmate.

312
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:36,754
This is Chao Yi-hsuan,
our new manager.

313
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:43,052
Lu-yung, have you eaten?
Why don't we have
dinner together?

314
00:21:46,472 --> 00:21:47,431
Okay.

315
00:21:49,517 --> 00:21:50,476
I want to go with you.

316
00:22:08,786 --> 00:22:10,579
Your manager is young.

317
00:22:10,704 --> 00:22:13,749
When you say "young",
I don't think it has
a positive meaning.

318
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:19,129
You think a young girl like me

319
00:22:19,380 --> 00:22:20,756
isn't qualified
to be a restaurant manager.

320
00:22:22,466 --> 00:22:24,509
There must be
some misunderstanding.

321
00:22:24,510 --> 00:22:27,721
I think you're young
and capable. I admire you.

322
00:22:28,389 --> 00:22:29,598
<i>You brat!</i>

323
00:22:31,517 --> 00:22:34,520
I heard you began to work
for Chang Xin before you even
graduated from college,

324
00:22:34,645 --> 00:22:36,020
and are still there at your age.

325
00:22:36,021 --> 00:22:37,481
<i>You old lady.</i>

326
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:43,987
You're high school classmates?

327
00:22:43,988 --> 00:22:44,989
Yeah.

328
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:47,992
So, you know Lu-yung's dad?

329
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:50,494
Uncle Jin-lai helped me a lot.

330
00:22:50,619 --> 00:22:52,663
I pay my respects
to him every year.

331
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:58,042
You're working
for the rival of my boss.

332
00:22:58,043 --> 00:23:00,754
How could you
still be his friend?

333
00:23:03,841 --> 00:23:05,467
- Yi-hsuan...
- Never mind.

334
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:08,846
What she said is true.

335
00:23:14,184 --> 00:23:15,935
To be honest,

336
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:17,729
we're forced
to transform ourselves

337
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:19,565
because Chang Xin
monopolizes the market.

338
00:23:19,690 --> 00:23:21,107
Don't pretend to be Virgin Mary.

339
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:23,861
In the <i>Doraemon</i> cartoon,
you're Shizuka.

340
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:27,489
What are you talking about?

341
00:23:32,912 --> 00:23:34,913
I was like you when I was young.

342
00:23:34,914 --> 00:23:37,750
I didn't have
much real-world experience,
so I was naive about everything.

343
00:23:38,417 --> 00:23:41,754
But you don't know some people
have their own reasons.

344
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:49,093
- Hsiu-wen is my high school
friend from long ago.
- Long ago?

345
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:50,721
It's high school, isn't it?

346
00:23:50,846 --> 00:23:53,724
Do you have to emphasize that?

347
00:23:54,516 --> 00:23:59,563
She works hard
to do the job she wants
and leads the life she wants.

348
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:00,898
I really respect her.

349
00:24:04,985 --> 00:24:06,236
Respect?

350
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:19,583
"As long as you keep
working hard,

351
00:24:21,251 --> 00:24:22,544
looking at you,

352
00:24:23,754 --> 00:24:25,839
I'll tell myself
not to give up."

353
00:24:35,683 --> 00:24:36,767
You wrote that to me
in a letter.

354
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,979
Whenever I think of it,

355
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:44,024
it seems I suddenly have
enough energy to keep working.

356
00:24:49,863 --> 00:24:52,491
Hello. Here's your pizza.

357
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:53,825
Okay.

358
00:24:53,826 --> 00:24:55,119
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

359
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:57,579
Let's eat.

360
00:25:00,791 --> 00:25:01,834
Come on.

361
00:25:02,835 --> 00:25:04,503
Smells good.

362
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:05,587
It smells good.

363
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:11,718
I'm sorry. I just remembered
that I have work to do.

364
00:25:11,719 --> 00:25:13,886
It's urgent.
I need to go back to the office.

365
00:25:13,887 --> 00:25:16,056
- Huh?
- I'm sorry.

366
00:25:16,598 --> 00:25:19,268
Stay, please.
Enjoy it while it's warm.

367
00:25:19,518 --> 00:25:20,853
I've got to go.

368
00:25:20,978 --> 00:25:22,187
Bye. See you next time.

369
00:25:23,313 --> 00:25:25,691
I've paid the bill.
Put your money away.

370
00:25:42,332 --> 00:25:43,625
You like her?

371
00:25:48,172 --> 00:25:49,173
Yeah.

372
00:25:50,174 --> 00:25:52,176
Excuse me. Can I get five shots?

373
00:25:53,552 --> 00:25:56,054
- Five?
- To punish you.

374
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:57,847
You're out drinking
with a cute girl like me,

375
00:25:57,848 --> 00:25:59,141
and you say
you like another girl.

376
00:26:05,981 --> 00:26:07,024
Bottoms up.

377
00:26:21,747 --> 00:26:23,207
Looks like the chain fell off.

378
00:26:30,756 --> 00:26:32,800
And your tire is flat.

379
00:26:34,051 --> 00:26:36,762
Are you alright?
You're hurt.

380
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:39,932
I'm fine.

381
00:26:40,057 --> 00:26:41,892
Wait here, I'll be right back.

382
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:43,894
There's a bicycle shop
around here.

383
00:26:44,019 --> 00:26:45,979
- I'll get you a new tire.
- Forget it. I'm late.

384
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:49,899
Are you sure?
I'll run over and get it.

385
00:26:49,900 --> 00:26:50,943
I'm already late.

386
00:26:55,197 --> 00:26:56,240
No. Wait!

387
00:26:56,907 --> 00:26:58,951
Why don't you call
to tell them you'll be late?

388
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:00,661
No. I'm never late.

389
00:27:01,370 --> 00:27:03,580
Maybe I'll carry you?

390
00:27:03,705 --> 00:27:04,915
No need.

391
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:06,708
It's annoying
if you run with me.

392
00:27:07,918 --> 00:27:09,127
Oh...

393
00:27:09,128 --> 00:27:10,379
I'm sorry.

394
00:27:18,178 --> 00:27:20,097
Got to go. Bye.

395
00:27:24,852 --> 00:27:26,061
You've carried it here?

396
00:27:27,146 --> 00:27:28,105
Yeah.

397
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:31,859
I'm sorry. I've fixed it,

398
00:27:34,653 --> 00:27:37,072
but I thought leaving it there
might be a bit risky.

399
00:27:39,408 --> 00:27:41,743
Don't tell me you've been
waiting here all day.

400
00:27:42,911 --> 00:27:45,705
No, I was home.

401
00:27:45,706 --> 00:27:46,999
I carried it here just now.

402
00:27:49,710 --> 00:27:50,669
Thanks.

403
00:27:54,464 --> 00:27:55,674
I'll get going.

404
00:27:55,799 --> 00:27:56,884
Yeah.

405
00:28:04,850 --> 00:28:05,809
Hey!

406
00:28:07,144 --> 00:28:08,729
Do you need help
with anything else?

407
00:28:12,149 --> 00:28:14,067
It's on my way.
Want to walk with me?

408
00:28:28,165 --> 00:28:29,708
Do you often go jogging here?

409
00:28:31,877 --> 00:28:32,920
Yeah.

410
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:35,380
It's breezy by the river.

411
00:28:36,757 --> 00:28:37,716
I love it.

412
00:28:41,303 --> 00:28:42,930
But I hate this place.

413
00:28:44,097 --> 00:28:45,182
Huh?

414
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:52,022
Whenever I'm here, I'm wondering
how much more I need to save,

415
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:53,440
how many shifts I should work.

416
00:29:05,077 --> 00:29:06,453
I want to study abroad.

417
00:29:08,288 --> 00:29:09,873
Where do you want to go?

418
00:29:13,252 --> 00:29:14,878
Where Uncle Jin-lai said

419
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:17,923
can make my future better.

420
00:29:20,968 --> 00:29:22,386
My dad is always right.

421
00:29:25,847 --> 00:29:27,057
I think you're cool.

422
00:29:32,229 --> 00:29:34,939
Whatever Chang Chien-yuen
had done,

423
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:36,817
nobody dared to stop him.

424
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:40,070
So, you're great.
You look cool.

425
00:29:42,781 --> 00:29:43,740
Um.

426
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:50,247
But looking at you and your dad,

427
00:29:54,418 --> 00:29:56,086
it makes me feel so small.

428
00:30:05,929 --> 00:30:07,222
But I don't think so.

429
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:11,435
You take care of your granny

430
00:30:12,853 --> 00:30:14,229
and work so hard to survive.

431
00:30:15,939 --> 00:30:17,941
I don't think you're small.

432
00:30:22,404 --> 00:30:23,530
I think you're...

433
00:30:29,953 --> 00:30:30,954
dazzling.

434
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:22,381
Don't you think the name
Jin Lai Hao is old-fashioned?

435
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:28,011
Jin-lai is my dad's name.

436
00:31:30,597 --> 00:31:32,432
This is our first restaurant.

437
00:31:33,517 --> 00:31:35,185
We named it together.

438
00:31:40,941 --> 00:31:42,359
You know, my first drink

439
00:31:44,194 --> 00:31:45,487
was with my dad.

440
00:31:54,454 --> 00:31:58,500
I didn't have a chance
to thank him properly.

441
00:32:18,019 --> 00:32:21,314
So, I want our restaurant
to be a place

442
00:32:22,607 --> 00:32:25,068
where people can come
with the ones they hold dear

443
00:32:26,069 --> 00:32:27,070
to their hearts.

444
00:32:41,710 --> 00:32:44,295
When you and your dad
opened the restaurant,

445
00:32:44,296 --> 00:32:45,630
was Hsiu-wen there?

446
00:32:47,674 --> 00:32:48,633
Yeah.

447
00:32:52,596 --> 00:32:54,639
I can't blame her then.

448
00:32:55,307 --> 00:32:58,351
What's to blame?
I was born too late.

449
00:33:16,453 --> 00:33:17,454
Boss?

450
00:33:56,618 --> 00:34:00,705
<i>I'm building castles
Castles in the sand</i>

451
00:34:00,830 --> 00:34:03,166
Back. Back, back, back.

452
00:34:05,335 --> 00:34:09,505
<i>I'm four years old
And I'm sat down with my dad</i>

453
00:34:09,506 --> 00:34:10,340
To your left.

454
00:34:10,465 --> 00:34:12,174
- Left?
- Yeah. Okay.

455
00:34:12,175 --> 00:34:13,343
- That's it.
- Yeah.

456
00:34:13,468 --> 00:34:15,511
Are you sure
we'll name it Jin Lai Hao?

457
00:34:15,512 --> 00:34:16,762
Better than "Yung's Place."

458
00:34:16,763 --> 00:34:19,181
But it feels strange
to use my own name.

459
00:34:19,182 --> 00:34:20,558
Wait.

460
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:23,394
- Yung's Place?
- Jin Lai Hao is better.

461
00:34:23,395 --> 00:34:25,814
Fine, Jin Lai Hao.
Jin Lai Hao.

462
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:27,565
Jin Lai Hao.

463
00:34:27,566 --> 00:34:28,608
JIN LAI HAO

464
00:34:31,486 --> 00:34:34,071
This is my secret recipe.

465
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:35,699
Hmm.

466
00:34:35,824 --> 00:34:37,199
2,000 dollars. Thank you.

467
00:34:37,200 --> 00:34:40,245
What? It's 20 dollars.

468
00:34:42,205 --> 00:34:45,292
<i>Lucky, I'm just a boy</i>

469
00:34:47,627 --> 00:34:48,837
Bye.

470
00:34:49,671 --> 00:34:53,215
By the way, have you received
my Police University
exam notice?

471
00:34:53,216 --> 00:34:55,467
I'm more nervous than you are.

472
00:34:55,468 --> 00:34:57,178
We'll celebrate when we get it.

473
00:34:58,263 --> 00:35:00,724
- Stay to the left.
- Okay.

474
00:35:03,602 --> 00:35:07,606
<i>I swim in rivers
Rivers that gone wild</i>

475
00:35:08,773 --> 00:35:10,400
GO FOR IT

476
00:35:11,860 --> 00:35:13,569
<i>I'm six years old</i>

477
00:35:13,570 --> 00:35:16,281
<i>And although
I'm just a child...</i>

478
00:35:16,406 --> 00:35:18,491
Hsiu-wen? Wu Hsiu-wen!

479
00:35:20,452 --> 00:35:22,245
Where are you going?
I'll give you a ride.

480
00:35:23,913 --> 00:35:25,457
No, thanks. I'm good.

481
00:35:25,582 --> 00:35:27,917
You're the first girl
I want to take for a ride.

482
00:35:40,555 --> 00:35:41,640
For you.

483
00:35:46,603 --> 00:35:48,271
- Is it good?
- Not bad.

484
00:35:49,648 --> 00:35:52,484
That's because you don't know
how to enjoy the best moment.

485
00:35:52,609 --> 00:35:53,902
Let's go!

486
00:35:57,489 --> 00:36:01,451
<i>My blue skies
And silver linings</i>

487
00:36:07,791 --> 00:36:09,626
Here. To happiness.

488
00:36:10,627 --> 00:36:11,794
Happiness!

489
00:36:11,795 --> 00:36:12,796
Cheers!

490
00:36:17,217 --> 00:36:19,177
Chef Jin-lai
just opened his own restaurant.

491
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:20,636
Many loyal customers

492
00:36:20,637 --> 00:36:22,347
trust his strict standards
for ingredients.

493
00:36:22,472 --> 00:36:23,973
They all go to eat there now.

494
00:36:24,224 --> 00:36:25,809
From the company's
operational perspective,

495
00:36:25,934 --> 00:36:28,478
I believe there's still plenty
of room for his capabilities

496
00:36:28,603 --> 00:36:30,480
to be put to good use
by Chang Xin.

497
00:36:30,939 --> 00:36:33,816
I suggest hiring him
as our Purchasing Manager.

498
00:36:33,817 --> 00:36:35,818
He can add great value
to the Chang Xin brand.

499
00:36:35,819 --> 00:36:40,323
Chang Xin was established
by Jin-lai,
your father, and me.

500
00:36:40,657 --> 00:36:42,700
Out of respect
for your late father,

501
00:36:42,701 --> 00:36:44,828
I allowed you
to persuade me once,

502
00:36:45,787 --> 00:36:48,289
but I don't want
to hear it again.

503
00:36:49,541 --> 00:36:51,376
As for "adding value
to the brand"?

504
00:36:52,877 --> 00:36:55,921
I built Chang Xin
to expand our territory,

505
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:58,216
not to fulfill some dream.

506
00:36:58,341 --> 00:37:00,260
He'll only hold Chang Xin back.

507
00:37:46,389 --> 00:37:47,348
Dad?

508
00:37:49,309 --> 00:37:50,268
Dad?

509
00:37:57,776 --> 00:38:00,987
TO CHOU LU-YUNG
GOOD JOB!

510
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:13,583
ENTRANCE EXAM ADMISSION TICKET

511
00:38:36,606 --> 00:38:39,484
JIN LAI HAO
CLOSED

512
00:38:56,626 --> 00:38:59,796
HANDSOME BOY

513
00:40:46,778 --> 00:40:47,737
Hi.

514
00:40:48,905 --> 00:40:51,156
I'm in charge
of your father's accident case.

515
00:40:51,157 --> 00:40:52,699
I'm Officer Wang.

516
00:40:52,700 --> 00:40:55,203
There are a few things
I'd like you to confirm.

517
00:40:55,954 --> 00:40:57,580
This morning,

518
00:40:58,706 --> 00:41:00,041
the offender turned himself in.

519
00:41:03,044 --> 00:41:05,755
He sincerely wants
to reach a settlement with you.

520
00:41:06,798 --> 00:41:07,966
Settlement?

521
00:41:08,091 --> 00:41:10,969
He thinks money
can pay for my dad's life?

522
00:41:11,761 --> 00:41:12,929
I know you're sad now.

523
00:41:13,054 --> 00:41:15,473
But I'm obligated to inform you.

524
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:17,100
Please take a look
at this document.

525
00:41:17,225 --> 00:41:18,601
I won't accept a settlement.

526
00:41:19,936 --> 00:41:21,187
Please leave.

527
00:41:23,064 --> 00:41:24,773
I'm sorry,
but I need to inform you...

528
00:41:24,774 --> 00:41:26,067
Can you please leave?

529
00:41:30,113 --> 00:41:33,533
Are you alright?
Sit down. Sit down.

530
00:41:34,951 --> 00:41:37,995
We're sorry, but he hasn't eaten
or slept for two days.

531
00:41:37,996 --> 00:41:39,497
Can you come back tomorrow?

532
00:41:40,707 --> 00:41:42,542
Take a look
at the document, please.

533
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:45,545
My condolences.

534
00:42:39,682 --> 00:42:41,559
Let go.

535
00:42:41,684 --> 00:42:42,643
See?

536
00:42:44,270 --> 00:42:45,313
Your birthday.

537
00:42:50,318 --> 00:42:52,028
This is Chang Chien-yuen's car.

538
00:42:57,241 --> 00:42:59,118
But the offender is this man.

539
00:43:05,041 --> 00:43:06,834
Are you sure it's his car?

540
00:43:11,923 --> 00:43:12,882
Yeah.

541
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:23,893
Lu-yung!
Where are you going, Lu-yung?

542
00:44:15,236 --> 00:44:17,280
You being this startled
makes it way too obvious.

543
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:33,713
You killed my dad, didn't you?

544
00:44:43,472 --> 00:44:44,682
What do you want?

545
00:45:23,763 --> 00:45:25,848
Why didn't you call
an ambulance?

546
00:45:25,973 --> 00:45:28,434
No. Listen, don't use violence.

547
00:45:31,354 --> 00:45:33,189
Why the hell
didn't you call an ambulance?

548
00:45:34,357 --> 00:45:37,067
I don't know. I don't know.

549
00:45:37,068 --> 00:45:38,360
I don't know.

550
00:45:38,361 --> 00:45:39,528
You don't know?

551
00:45:49,872 --> 00:45:51,249
He was my dad.

552
00:45:53,125 --> 00:45:54,543
He was my dad!

553
00:45:58,047 --> 00:45:59,966
You left him there all alone.

554
00:46:00,925 --> 00:46:02,927
Who do you think you are?

555
00:46:13,020 --> 00:46:14,563
Who do you think you are?

556
00:46:25,574 --> 00:46:27,410
Help.

557
00:46:27,535 --> 00:46:29,036
Help me.

558
00:46:36,544 --> 00:46:39,088
You killed my dad
because I hit you?

559
00:46:40,214 --> 00:46:41,423
Answer me!

560
00:46:41,424 --> 00:46:42,425
I'm sorry.

561
00:46:44,343 --> 00:46:45,886
I'm sorry.

562
00:46:49,807 --> 00:46:52,100
I'm sorry.

563
00:46:52,101 --> 00:46:53,936
Why weren't you
the one who died?

564
00:46:55,104 --> 00:46:57,356
Why weren't you
the one who died?

565
00:47:36,354 --> 00:47:37,605
Go to hell!

566
00:47:45,988 --> 00:47:47,322
Freeze!

567
00:47:47,323 --> 00:47:48,323
Put down the stone!

568
00:47:48,324 --> 00:47:49,325
Lu-yung!

569
00:47:51,994 --> 00:47:53,162
I repeat.

570
00:47:53,913 --> 00:47:55,164
Put down the stone.

571
00:47:55,998 --> 00:47:57,666
He killed my dad.

572
00:47:57,917 --> 00:47:59,250
I'm going to kill him!

573
00:47:59,251 --> 00:48:01,419
Lu-yung,

574
00:48:01,420 --> 00:48:04,507
do you want to become a murderer
because of Chang Chien-yuen?

575
00:48:06,175 --> 00:48:07,426
Listen to your friend.

576
00:48:08,302 --> 00:48:10,888
Even if you kill him now,
your dad won't be alive again.

577
00:48:13,099 --> 00:48:14,432
I promise you

578
00:48:14,433 --> 00:48:16,310
I'll resume
the investigation, okay?

579
00:48:17,561 --> 00:48:18,896
Put down the stone.

580
00:48:27,530 --> 00:48:29,573
What are you talking about?

581
00:48:30,658 --> 00:48:32,493
What are you saying?

582
00:48:34,203 --> 00:48:35,538
- Freeze!
- Wait! No!

583
00:48:35,663 --> 00:48:37,540
- What are you doing?
- Wait! Don't shoot!

584
00:48:37,665 --> 00:48:39,041
Wait, please.

585
00:48:39,166 --> 00:48:40,126
Don't shoot!

586
00:48:43,212 --> 00:48:44,462
Don't shoot!

587
00:48:44,463 --> 00:48:47,632
Please! Don't shoot, please.

588
00:48:47,633 --> 00:48:49,135
Don't shoot!

589
00:48:50,428 --> 00:48:51,512
Hsiu-wen?

590
00:48:55,558 --> 00:48:57,059
Let him do it.

591
00:48:58,227 --> 00:48:59,937
I don't give a damn.

592
00:49:04,066 --> 00:49:06,652
Are you crazy, Chou Lu-yung?

593
00:49:09,196 --> 00:49:12,240
Uncle Jin-lai wouldn't want you
to kill anyone!

594
00:49:12,241 --> 00:49:15,286
Or see you killed here!

595
00:49:16,704 --> 00:49:19,457
He would never want you
to seek revenge for him

596
00:49:19,582 --> 00:49:22,042
and ruin your life.

597
00:49:23,752 --> 00:49:27,214
If he were here,
he would never want to see that.

598
00:49:32,219 --> 00:49:34,263
Live on, okay?

599
00:49:35,598 --> 00:49:36,682
Otherwise...

600
00:49:38,601 --> 00:49:39,602
Otherwise...

601
00:49:42,396 --> 00:49:47,109
Otherwise, Uncle Jin-lai will
truly be gone, Chou Lu-yung.

602
00:50:50,172 --> 00:50:51,173
A new guy.

603
00:50:57,805 --> 00:50:59,098
Keep your head down.
